"""HELD-OUT receipts -- never used while developing the extraction rules.

`ibg_corpus.py` is the training corpus: its 28 samples were in front of the
developers while they wrote the rules, so a 100% score on it is an *in-sample*
score and says nothing about generalization.

This file is the control. Every sample here comes from a receipt the owner
supplied that was NOT transcribed into the corpus and that no rule was ever
tuned against. Scoring against it is the honest measure of whether the label
vocabulary generalizes to unseen documents from the same banks.

Keep it that way: **do not fix a failure by editing this file, and do not move a
sample from here into the corpus.** If a held-out sample fails, either fix the
rule so it generalizes, or record the failure. Moving the goalposts here
destroys the only unbiased measurement available.

Expected values were read off the source PDFs by hand.
"""

from app.ibg.contract import (
    ROLE_BANK_PRIMARY as PRIMARY,
    ROLE_BANK_SECONDARY as SECONDARY,
    ROLE_PAYER_SUPPLIED as PAYER,
)

